r by provider and model generation. Name each artifact's owner and a reference that can't change, where one exists. A machine-readable format, such as CycloneDX ML-BOM or the SPDX 3.0 AI and Dataset profiles, lets tools check the manifest.\n15\t\n16\tIf a check fails, also copy the words from this requirement that the code breaks into\n17\t`violates`. Then write your answer (format at the end).\n18\t\n19\t\n20\t## C01.1\n21\t\n22\t**Check:** A release manifest file lists the container, harness, system prompt, rules files, model, built-in tools, MCP servers, permission scopes, memory and retrieval settings, identity bindings, network rules, execution budgets, and security-policy versions.\n23\t\n24\t**How to verify:** 1) Find the release manifest (`.brace/manifest.yaml`, release manifest, ML-BOM). 2) Check each category: container, harness, system prompt, rules files, model, built-in tools, MCP servers, permission scopes, memory and retrieval, identity bindings, network rules, budgets, security-policy versions. 3) Compare with what config sets up (`*.mcp.json`, NetworkPolicy). 4) Answer no if any category is missing or configured items are left out.\n25\t\n26\t**Reviewer's evidence:** release/manifest.json:65 — \"\"policies\": { \"action\": \"config/policy.yaml\", \"actionPolicyVersion\": \"2026-09-18.3\" }\"\n27\t\n28\t**Reviewer's note:** Manifest covers each required category\n29\t\n30\t`release/manifest.json` lines 53–66 (cited lines marked >):\n31\t```\n32\t  53      }\n33\t  54    ],\n34\t  55    \"permissions\": {\n35\t  56      \"awsRole\": \"arn:aws:iam::418295730611:role/clinic-agent-runtime\",\n36\t  57      \"ehrScopes\": [\"patient.read\", \"appointment.read\", \"appointment.write\"],\n37\t  58      \"paymentsScopes\": [\"deposits.refund\"],\n38\t  59      \"eligibilityScopes\": [\"eligibility:read\"]\n39\t  60    },\n40\t  61    \"memory\": \"none\",\n41\t  62    \"retrieval\": \"none\",\n42\t  63    \"network\": { \"policy\": \"k8s/deployment.yaml#clin